<section class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">YOUR PRIVACY MATTERS</p><h1>Safe reporting and handover.</h1><p class="lead">A few practical rules help keep the campus lost-and-found process safe and reliable.</p></section>
<section class="safety-list"><article><h2>Keep proof private</h2><p>Use the private-details field for distinguishing information. Do not publish every identifying mark in the public description.</p></article><article><h2>Meet in a sensible place</h2><p>Arrange handover in a busy, familiar campus location or follow official campus security guidance. If anything feels unsafe, ask university staff for help.</p></article><article><h2>Protect personal information</h2><p>Do not post passwords, PINs, full bank-card numbers, identity-document numbers, or private contact details in a report.</p></article><article><h2>Report suspicious claims</h2><p>Do not hand over an item based only on a message. Verify ownership using details only the genuine owner is likely to know.</p></article></section>
<div class="note">This is a campus community tool, not an emergency service. For urgent security concerns, contact the appropriate university security office.</div>
